n10. fix this \n\nTraining (QLoRA)\tCell 6 (bBtUZIG4wjco)\t⚠️ Overfitted\t60 steps in 5m26s. Loss = 0.0032 (needs 2 epochs instead of 5)\n\n<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **Core Request:** Fix the overfitting issue in Cell 6 (`bBtUZIG4wjco`) of the training notebook `Fluxnat_Coder_3B_Training.ipynb` (Colab URL: `https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1u6mCyiyeT45QW6O0L-95tJ-csN6VEC17#scrollTo=bBtUZIG4wjco`).\n- **Success Criteria:** Update the training parameters, dataset balance, and code in `Fluxnat_Coder_3B_Training.ipynb` (and local training scripts `train.py`, `config/training_config.yaml`) so the model trains for 2 epochs instead of 5, maintains healthy entropy (target loss ~0.60–0.80 instead of 0.0032), avoids rote memorization, and introduces negative benign samples so it stops classifying clean code as vulnerable.\n- **Constraints:**\n  - Absolute zero mention of \"Qwen\", \"qwen2\", or \"Alibaba\" anywhere in code, markdown, configurations, datasets, or outputs.\n  - Zero Ollama dependency.\n  - Retain refusal-free / uncensored security auditing personality.\n  - Keep training executable on free Google Colab (Tesla T4 GPU 16GB VRAM) and local inference executable on 4GB GTX 1650.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Completed:**\n  - Full codebase forensic scrub: 0 occurrences of base model name across all repository files (`smartagent/config.py`, `train.py`, `evaluate.py`, `merge_and_export.py`, `prepare_datasets.py`, `README.md`, `Fluxnat_Coder_3B_Training.ipynb`, and all JSONL datasets).\n  - Published model on Hugging Face: `https://huggingface.co/k4ran909/Fluxnat-Coder-3B` with custom architecture `configuration_fluxnat.py` and `modeling_fluxnat.py`.\n  - Local inference environment configured on Windows in Python 3.12 (`torch-2.6.0+cu124`, `transformers-5.17.0`, `accelerate-1.15.0`).\n  - Executed local tests (`test_local_model.py` and `test_refusal_free.py`): Verified 100% zero-refusal behavior across SQLi AST, reverse shell deconstruction, and buffer overflow mechanics.\n  - Executed benchmark suite (`benchmark_suite.py`): Identified 87.5% vulnerability detection recall, but 0% false positive resistance (flags all clean code as critical vulnerabilities) and defaulting to CWE-22 due to the severe overfitting in Cell 6.\n  - Audited Colab training run: Confirmed training finished 60 steps in 5m26s with loss 1.79 -> 0.0032 (5 epochs on 90 samples, 119.7M trainable parameters, LoRA $r=64$, $\\alpha=128$).\n- **In Progress:** Updating Cell 6 (`bBtUZIG4wjco`) and associated dataset/training configurations in `Fluxnat_Coder_3B_Training.ipynb` and local project files to resolve the overfitting and false positive bias.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings & Decisions\n- **Root Cause of Cell 6 Overfitting:**\n  1. `Num examples = 90` with `Num Epochs = 5` ($90 \\times 5 = 450$ passes) caused the model to memorize exact token strings.\n  2. LoRA rank $r=64$ ($\\alpha=128$) created 119.7M trainable parameters—vastly oversized for only 90 short text samples.\n  3. The dataset contained **zero benign/safe samples**, causing the model to learn an inductive prior that all code is Critical CVSS 9.8.\n- **Specific Fix Parameters:**\n  - `num_train_epochs = 2` (or `max_steps = 25` down from 60).\n  - `learning_rate = 1e-4` (down from 2e-4).\n  - Add 40–50 benign / safe code samples (`Status: BENIGN / SECURE`) to Step 4 dataset creation.\n  - Set LoRA rank $r=16$ or $r=32$ ($\\alpha=32$ or $\\alpha=64$) when dataset is under 200 samples.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Active Context\n- Local workspace: `c:\\Users\\k4ran\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\smartAGENT`.\n- Notebook file: `Fluxnat_Coder_3B_Training.ipynb`.\n- Python 3.14 (`C:\\Python314\\python.exe`) for scripts; Python 3.12 (`C:\\Users\\k4ran\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\Python\\Python312\\python.exe`) for PyTorch/Transformers inference.\n- Colab session: User has `Fluxnat_Coder_3B_Training.ipynb` open in Google Colab.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Next Steps (In Priority Order)\n1. **Update `Fluxnat_Coder_3B_Training.ipynb`:**\n   - Modify Step 4 (Dataset Preparation) to add negative benign/secure code examples (`Status: BENIGN / SECURE. No vulnerabilities detected`) alongside the security CoT and identity records.\n   - Modify Step 5 / Cell 6 (`bBtUZIG4wjco` TrainingArguments):\n     - Change `max_steps = 25` (or `num_train_epochs = 2`).\n     - Adjust `learning_rate = 1e-4` or `5e-5`.\n     - Lower LoRA rank in Step 3 to $r=16$, $\\alpha=32$ to prevent capacity bloat.\n2. **Update Local Training & Config Files:**\n   - Update `config/training_config.yaml` (`epochs: 2`, `r: 16`, `lora_alpha: 32`, `learning_rate: 1.0e-4`).\n   - Update `train.py` and `prepare_datasets.py` with the balanced benign dataset generation.\n3. **Present Updated Cell Code & Instructions to User:**\n   - Provide the exact replacement code for Cell 4, Cell 5, and Cell 6 in their Colab notebook.\n   - Advise them to run the calibrated 2-epoch training in Colab (takes ~90 seconds) to obtain target loss ~0.60–0.80 and achieve 90%+ benchmark accuracy.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Commitments & Constraints\n- Absolutely no mention of \"Qwen\" in code, explanations, or artifacts.\n- Keep the model completely refusal-free for cybersecurity research.\n</summary>\n\nYou have the 8 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: agent]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/k4ran/.gemini/antigravity/brain/e2c1cf9f-2dff-4bf4-a974-ef410441acfa/.agents/agents/file-writer/agent.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T20:38:34Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: best_slm_comparison]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/k4ran/.gemini/antigravity/brain/e2c1cf9f-2dff-4bf4-a974-ef410441acfa/best_slm_comparison.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T19:47:46Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: best_slm_under_4b]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/k4ran/.gemini/antigravity/brain/e2c1cf9f-2dff-4bf4-a974-ef410441acfa/best_slm_under_4b.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T19:50:32Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: best_uncensored_under_3b]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/k4ran/.gemini/antigravity/brain/e2c1cf9f-2dff-4bf4-a974-ef410441acfa/best_uncensore